growth journey by leveraging its TMT and software expertise, global platform and cross-pollination opportunities with IFS, with Acumatica operating as a sister company to IFS.","value_creation_source_url":"https://eqtgroup.com/news/eqt-acquires-acumatica-a-us-based-cloud-native-erp-software-vendor-in-connection-with-its-existing-ifs-investment-2019-06-19","notes":"EQT VII acquired majority ownership in 2019 from the founders, management and minority investors, who re-invested significantly. EQT's portfolio page now titles it 'Former EQT Portfolio Company'. Exit announced 2025-05-29: during EQT's ownership headcount grew more than 3x and revenue 7x."}},{"name":"Khazna Data Centers","website":"https://khaznadatacenters.com/","description":"Khazna Data Centers designs, builds and operates hyperscale data centers, enabling the growth of AI and digital economies by delivering advanced, energy-efficient infrastructure for high-density computing.","sector":"Digital infrastructure","subsector":"Hyperscale wholesale data centers","country":"United Arab Emirates","business_model":"B2B (wholesale/hyperscale colocation)","email":"info@khazna.ae","email_type":"generic","leaders":[{"role":"ceo","name":"Hassan Alnaqbi","title":"Chief Executive Officer","source_url":"https://khaznadatacenters.com/about-us/","source_kind":"company","evidence":"Leadership Team | Hassan Alnaqbi | Chief Executive Officer"},{"role":"cfo","name":"Fabio Cattaneo","title":"Chief Financial Officer","source_url":"https://khaznadatacenters.com/about-us/","source_kind":"company","evidence":"Fabio Cattaneo | Chief Financial Officer"},{"role":"managing_director","name":"Bart Holsters","title":"Managing Director – Khazna NexOps","source_url":"https://khaznadatacenters.com/about-us/","source_kind":"company","evidence":"Bart Holsters | Managing Director – Khazna NexOps"},{"role":"other","name":"Abdulmajeed Harmoodi","title":"Chief Technology Officer","source_url":"https://khaznadatacenters.com/about-us/","source_kind":"company","evidence":"Abdulmajeed Harmoodi | Chief Technology Officer"},{"role":"other","name":"Gregory Jasmin","title":"Chief Commercial Officer","source_url":"https://khaznadatacenters.com/about-us/","source_kind":"company","evidence":"Gregory Jasmin | Chief Commercial Officer"}],"notes":"Shareholders listed on its site: G42 (majority), MGX and Silver Lake. e& exited its stake when MGX and Silver Lake came in (March 2025). Facilities across the UAE (AUH6 retrofitted for GPU workloads; Ajman to add 100MW of AI-capable capacity). No employee count, revenue or EBITDA disclosed.","sources":{"description":{"url":"https://khaznadatacenters.com/about-us/","name":"Khazna Data Centers","kind":"company","as_of":null,"evidence":"With one of fastest-expanding platforms of hyperscale data centers globally, Khazna Data Centers enables the growth of artificial intelligence (AI) and digital economies by delivering advanced infrastructure with unparalleled energy efficiency."},"country":{"url":"https://khaznadatacenters.com/press-release/khazna-welcomes-mgx-and-silver-lake-as-strategic-minority-investors/","name":"Khazna Data Centers","kind":"company","as_of":"2025-03-26","evidence":"Dubai, UAE, 26 March, 2025 – Khazna Data Centers is proud to welcome MGX and Silver Lake as new minority shareholders"},"business_model":{"url":"https://www.silverlake.com/portfolio/khazna-data-centers/","name":"Silver Lake","kind":"sponsor","as_of":null,"evidence":"Khazna Data Centers is the largest hyperscale wholesale data center provider in the Middle East and North Africa."},"email":{"url":"https://khaznadatacenters.com/contact-us/","name":"Khazna Data Centers","kind":"company","as_of":null,"evidence":"Inquiry | info@khazna.ae | Phone | +971 4 556 0204"}},"holding":{"sponsor":"Silver Lake","status":"current","status_note":"Minority shareholder since 2025 alongside majority owner G42 and MGX","asset_class":"Private equity","deal_type":"Minority stake","value_creation_plan":"Khazna said the support of MGX and Silver Lake positions it to accelerate its global expansion plans and enhance its AI-optimized capabilities.","value_creation_source_url":"https://khaznadatacenters.com/press-release/khazna-welcomes-mgx-and-silver-lake-as-strategic-minority-investors/","notes":"Announced 2025-03-26 by Khazna; Silver Lake lists 'Partner Since 2025', strategy 'Silver Lake Partners & Alpine', Current Investment, Data Centers & Networking. Stake size and price not disclosed. The value-creation line is Khazna's statement; Silver Lake published no separate plan."}},{"name":"Baker Tilly","website":"https://www.bakertilly.com/","description":"Baker Tilly is a leading advisory, tax and assurance firm serving the middle market, operating through Baker Tilly Advisory Group, LP (tax and business advisory) and Baker Tilly US, LLP (a licensed CPA firm providing attest services).","sector":"Professional services","subsector":"Accounting, audit, tax and advisory (CPA firm)","country":"United States","business_model":"B2B professional services","leaders":[{"role":"ceo","name":"Eric Miles","title":"Chief Executive Officer","source_url":"https://www.bakertilly.com/news/baker-tilly-announces-eric-miles-as-chief-executive-officer","source_kind":"company","evidence":"CHICAGO (Jan. 7, 2026) — Baker Tilly, a leading advisory, tax and assurance firm, today announced that Eric Miles has assumed the role of chief executive officer, succeeding Jeff Ferro."},{"role":"cfo","name":"Sonia Webb","title":"Chief Financial Officer","source_url":"https://www.bakertilly.com/news/baker-tilly-announces-new-senior-leadership-team","source_kind":"company","evidence":"With these appointments, Baker Tilly’s Senior Leadership Team will include: ... • Sonia Webb, Chief Financial Officer (structure effective Jan. 1, 2026)"},{"role":"coo","name":"Fred Massanova","title":"North American Managing Principal and Chief Operating Officer","source_url":"https://www.bakertilly.com/news/baker-tilly-announces-new-senior-leadership-team","source_kind":"company","evidence":"Fred Massanova has been named North American Managing Principal and Chief Operating Officer."}],"notes":"Headquartered in Chicago (press-release dateline). Combined with Moss Adams in June 2025 (announced 2025-04-21 as creating the sixth largest advisory CPA firm in the US). Under the alternative practice structure H&F holds no equity in the audit and attest business (Baker Tilly US, LLP); partners hold equity alongside H&F and Valeas in Baker Tilly Advisory Group, LP. Member of Baker Tilly International (network-wide revenue USD 7bn; not this firm's revenue). No firm-level revenue, EBITDA or headcount opened from an accepted source.","sources":{"description":{"url":"https://www.bakertilly.com/news/baker-tilly-announces-eric-miles-as-chief-executive-officer","name":"Baker Tilly","kind":"company","as_of":"2026-01-07","evidence":"Baker Tilly is a leading advisory, tax and assurance firm ... Baker Tilly US, LLP, is a licensed independent CPA firm that provides attest services to its clients. Baker Tilly Advisory Group, LP, and its subsidiary entities provide tax and business advisory services to their clients."},"country":{"url":"https://www.bakertilly.com/news/baker-tilly-announces-eric-miles-as-chief-executive-officer","name":"Baker Tilly","kind":"company","as_of":"2026-01-07","evidence":"CHICAGO (Jan. 7, 2026) — Baker Tilly, a leading advisory, tax and assurance firm"},"business_model":{"url":"https://hf.com/portfolio/baker-tilly/","name":"Hellman & Friedman","kind":"sponsor","as_of":"2024-06-05","evidence":"a leading US Advisory CPA firm, performing audit, tax and advisory services, and primarily serving middle market clients"}},"holding":{"sponsor":"Hellman & Friedman","status":"current","status_note":"Investor since June 2024 (with Valeas); made a further strategic investment with the 2025 Moss Adams combination","asset_class":"Private equity","value_creation_plan":"H&F said it would invest alongside Baker Tilly's partners and senior leadership to bolster its capabilities, expand its footprint and help build the country's preeminent mid-market advisory CPA firm, giving it capital to accelerate growth through talent, technology and strategic acquisitions.","value_creation_source_url":"https://www.bakertilly.com/news/baker-tilly-secures-strategic-investment-led-by-hellman","notes":"Announced 2024-02-05 as the largest private equity investment in the US CPA sector to date; closed in June 2024 (H&F news dated 2024-06-05). H&F made a meaningful additional investment in the 2025 Baker Tilly-Moss Adams merger. Stake size not stated in the sources read, so deal type left blank."}},{"name":"Opella","website":"https://www.opella.com/","description":"Opella is a consumer healthcare company and the third-largest business worldwide in over-the-counter medicines and vitamins, minerals & supplements, with brands such as Allegra, Doliprane and Dulcolax serving more than half a billion consumers.","sector":"Healthcare","subsector":"Consumer healthcare (OTC and VMS)","country":"France","business_model":"B2C (consumer health brands)","email":"contact@opella.com","email_type":"generic","employees":11000,"employees_text":"Opella employs over 11,000 talented and passionate people","employees_as_of":"2025-04-30","revenue":4600000000,"revenue_currency":"EUR","revenue_period":"FY2025","leaders":[{"role":"ceo","name":"Julie Van Ongevalle","title":"Opella President & Chief Executive Officer","source_url":"https://www.opella.com/en/meet-opella/our-leaders","source_kind":"company","evidence":"Julie Van Ongevalle. Opella President & Chief Executive Officer."},{"role":"cfo","name":"Adeline Le Franc","title":"Chief Financial Officer","source_url":"https://www.opella.com/en/meet-opella/our-leaders","source_kind":"company","evidence":"Adeline Le Franc. Chief Financial Officer."},{"role":"other","name":"Rafik Amrane","title":"Chief Supply Chain Officer","source_url":"https://www.opella.com/en/meet-opella/our-leaders","source_kind":"company","evidence":"Rafik Amrane. Chief Supply Chain Officer."},{"role":"other","name":"Greg Ross","title":"President of North America","source_url":"https://www.opella.com/en/meet-opella/our-leaders","source_kind":"company","evidence":"Greg Ross. President of North America."},{"role":"other","name":"Gonzalo Balcazar","title":"President of Europe and Latin America","source_url":"https://www.opella.com/en/meet-opella/our-leaders","source_kind":"company","evidence":"Gonzalo Balcazar. President of Europe and Latin America."},{"role":"other","name":"Carol-Ann Stewart","title":"President of Asia Pacific, Middle East, Africa","source_url":"https://www.opella.com/en/meet-opella/our-leaders","source_kind":"company","evidence":"Carol-Ann Stewart. President of Asia Pacific, Middle East, Africa."}],"notes":"Former consumer healthcare business of Sanofi; independent since 2025-04-30. Operates in 100 countries with 13 manufacturing sites and four science and innovation development centers. Revenue is the company's rounded figure ('€4.6bn revenues in 2025', footnoted 'Opella data, FY 2025 published financial results'). Sanofi's FY2024 filing reported Opella sales of EUR 4,948m 'under the new scope of reporting' (the two are not on the same scope). No EBITDA figure found from an accepted source.","sources":{"description":{"url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1121404/000119312525106923/d935542dex991.htm","name":"Sanofi press release (Form 6-K, SEC)","kind":"filing","as_of":"2025-04-30","evidence":"With a portfolio of iconic brands, such as Allegra, Doliprane, and Dulcolax, Opella is already the third-largest business worldwide in the over-the-counter and vitamins, minerals & supplements market (OTC & VMS), serving more than half a billion consumers worldwide."},"employees":{"url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1121404/000119312525106923/d935542dex991.htm","name":"Sanofi press release (Form 6-K, SEC)","kind":"filing","as_of":"2025-04-30","evidence":"Headquartered in France, Opella employs over 11,000 talented and passionate people, operates in 100 countries with 13 best-in-class and strategic manufacturing sites and four science and innovation development centers."},"revenue":{"url":"https://www.opella.com/en","name":"Opella","kind":"company","as_of":null,"evidence":"€4.6bn revenues 2 in 2025. ... Sources ... Opella data, FY 2025 published financial results."},"country":{"url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1121404/000119312525106923/d935542dex991.htm","name":"Sanofi press release (Form 6-K, SEC)","kind":"filing","as_of":"2025-04-30","evidence":"Headquartered in France, Opella employs over 11,000 talented and passionate people"},"business_model":{"url":"https://www.opella.com/en","name":"Opella","kind":"company","as_of":null,"evidence":"We're making self-care as simple as it should be. ... #3 leading OTC & VMS global player"},"email":{"url":"https://www.opella.com/en/contact","name":"Opella","kind":"company","as_of":null,"evidence":"contact@opella.com | Drop us a line."}},"holding":{"sponsor":"Clayton, Dubilier & Rice, LLC","status":"current","status_note":"Acquired a 50.0% controlling stake from Sanofi, closed 2025-04-30 (Sanofi retains 48.2%, Bpifrance 1.8%)","asset_class":"Private equity","deal_type":"Carve-out","value_creation_plan":"CD&R said it will support Opella in building a French-headquartered global consumer health champion, bringing consumer health experience, operational insight and long-term capital to help accelerate Opella's growth in France and abroad.","value_creation_source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1121404/000119312525106923/d935542dex991.htm","notes":"Sanofi received total net cash proceeds of around EUR 10 billion. CD&R lists Investment Date 2025, Region Europe, Sector Healthcare. Quote from Eric Rouzier, Partner and Head of European Healthcare, CD&R."}},{"name":"SILA","website":"https://silagroup.co.in/","description":"SILA is a business services and real estate platform in India delivering integrated, tech-enabled facility management, material handling equipment leasing, food catering and real estate advisory and development for corporates, funds and developers.","sector":"Business services","subsector":"Integrated facility management and real estate services","country":"India","founded_year":2010,"business_model":"B2B services","employees":60000,"employees_text":"a workforce exceeding 60,000","employees_as_of":"2026-04-08","leaders":[{"role":"managing_director","name":"Rushabh Vora","title":"Co-Founder & Managing Director","source_url":"https://silagroup.co.in/about-us/","source_kind":"company","evidence":"Meet our Leadership Team | Sahil Vora | Founder | Rushabh Vora | Co-Founder & Managing Director"},{"role":"cfo","name":"Milind Pattarkine","title":"Chief Financial Officer","source_url":"https://silagroup.co.in/about-us/","source_kind":"company","evidence":"Milind Pattarkine | Chief Financial Officer"},{"role":"other","name":"Sahil Vora","title":"Founder","source_url":"https://silagroup.co.in/about-us/","source_kind":"company","evidence":"Founder | Sahil Vora | SILA was founded with a vision to build a trusted business services and real estate platform"},{"role":"other","name":"Raghav Kapur","title":"Executive Director - Services","source_url":"https://silagroup.co.in/about-us/","source_kind":"company","evidence":"Raghav Kapur | Executive Director - Services"},{"role":"other","name":"Vinay Deshmukh","title":"CEO & Executive Director, FFServices","source_url":"https://silagroup.co.in/about-us/","source_kind":"company","evidence":"Vinay Deshmukh | CEO & Executive Director, FFServices"}],"notes":"Corporate office: A-301, Neelam Centre, Hind Cycle Marg, Worli, Mumbai. Operates across 125+ cities in India managing over 450 million sq ft of real estate. Founded April 2010 as a facility management company; acquired Forbes Facility Management Services from the Shapoorji Pallonji Group (2022) and SMS from Samara Capital (Jan 2026). SILA lists no group CEO; the founder brothers lead it. Only role-specific emails (marketing@, recruitment@) are published, so none recorded. No revenue or EBITDA figure disclosed (site states '10x revenue growth within 5 years').","sources":{"description":{"url":"https://www.permira.com/news-and-insights/announcements/sila-announces-strategic-investment-from-permira","name":"Permira","kind":"sponsor","as_of":"2026-04-08","evidence":"The company delivers integrated, tech-enabled services spanning facility management, material handling equipment leasing, food catering, and real estate advisory — serving large corporates, funds, and developers across the full asset lifecycle."},"employees":{"url":"https://www.permira.com/news-and-insights/announcements/sila-announces-strategic-investment-from-permira","name":"Permira","kind":"sponsor","as_of":"2026-04-08","evidence":"SILA today operates across 125+ cities in India, managing over 450 million square feet of real estate with a workforce exceeding 60,000."},"founded_year":{"url":"https://silagroup.co.in/about-us/","name":"SILA","kind":"company","as_of":null,"evidence":"April 2010 | Founded SILA as a Facility Management company"},"country":{"url":"https://silagroup.co.in/contact-us/","name":"SILA","kind":"company","as_of":null,"evidence":"Corporate Office | A - 301, Neelam Centre, Hind Cycle Marg, Worli, Mumbai - 400030"},"business_model":{"url":"https://www.permira.com/news-and-insights/announcements/sila-announces-strategic-investment-from-permira","name":"Permira","kind":"sponsor","as_of":"2026-04-08","evidence":"serving large corporates, funds, and developers across the full asset lifecycle"}},"holding":{"sponsor":"Permira","status":"current","status_note":"USD 100 million strategic investment by Permira funds, announced April 2026","asset_class":"Private equity","value_creation_plan":"The investment will support SILA's continued expansion across India by strengthening its technology capabilities, expanding adjacent service lines and pursuing growth opportunities, with Permira bringing its global pattern recognition, internal operator bench and international networks.","value_creation_source_url":"https://www.permira.com/news-and-insights/announcements/sila-announces-strategic-investment-from-permira","notes":"Announced 2026-04-08; Norwest Venture Partners keeps a meaningful minority position. SILA's site records 'April 2026 SILA Services received US$100 mm investment from Permira'. Permira's stake size not stated in the sources read, so deal type left blank."}},{"name":"Regenity Biosciences","website":"https://regenity.com/","description":"Regenity Biosciences is a global developer and manufacturer of bioresorbable technologies and biomaterials that support tissue and bone regeneration across dental, orthopaedic, spine, neurosurgery, advanced wound, sports medicine, ENT and nerve repair.","sector":"Healthcare","subsector":"Medical devices / regenerative biomaterials (contract development and manufacturing)","country":"United States","founded_year":1997,"business_model":"B2B (develops and manufactures products for strategic customers)","employees":250,"employees_text":"the Company’s team of over 250 employees","employees_as_of":"2026-02-12","leaders":[{"role":"ceo","name":"Shawn McCarthy","title":"Chief Executive Officer","source_url":"https://regenity.com/about-regenity/","source_kind":"company","evidence":"Our Team | Leaders. Trailblazers. Partners. | Shawn McCarthy | Chief Executive Officer"},{"role":"cfo","name":"Oystein Valberg","title":"Chief Financial Officer","source_url":"https://regenity.com/about-regenity/","source_kind":"company","evidence":"Oystein Valberg | Chief Financial Officer"},{"role":"coo","name":"Aaron Kendrick","title":"Senior Vice President, Operations","source_url":"https://regenity.com/about-regenity/","source_kind":"company","evidence":"Aaron Kendrick | Senior Vice President, Operations"}],"notes":"Headquarters: 115 W. Century Rd, Suite 380, Paramus, New Jersey; manufacturing facility in Allendale, NJ. Serves more than 125 customers with 80+ product lines; over 100 patents; more than 5 million patients treated in 2025. Previously and still backed by Linden Capital Partners. COO slot holds the SVP Operations, the nearest operations title. No published generic email (only a QA support desk address), revenue or EBITDA.","sources":{"description":{"url":"https://www.cinven.com/news-insights/regenity-biosciences-announcement/","name":"Cinven","kind":"sponsor","as_of":"2026-02-12","evidence":"Regenity has spent nearly 30 years advancing innovative biomaterials that support the body’s natural healing processes for tissue and bone regeneration across multiple clinical areas, including dental, orthopaedic, spine, neurosurgery, advanced wound, sports medicine, ENT, and nerve repair."},"employees":{"url":"https://www.cinven.com/news-insights/regenity-biosciences-announcement/","name":"Cinven","kind":"sponsor","as_of":"2026-02-12","evidence":"Today, the Company’s team of over 250 employees serves more than 125 customers with 80+ product lines globally."},"founded_year":{"url":"https://www.cinven.com/news-insights/regenity-biosciences-announcement/","name":"Cinven","kind":"sponsor","as_of":"2026-02-12","evidence":"Founded in 1997 and headquartered in New Jersey, USA"},"country":{"url":"https://regenity.com/contact-us/","name":"Regenity Biosciences","kind":"company","as_of":null,"evidence":"Headquarters | 115 W. Century Rd | Suite 380 | Paramus, New Jersey | 07652 USA"},"business_model":{"url":"https://www.cinven.com/news-insights/regenity-biosciences-announcement/","name":"Cinven","kind":"sponsor","as_of":"2026-02-12","evidence":"developing and commercializing innovative products and next-generation technologies alongside its strategic customers"}},"holding":{"sponsor":"Cinven","status":"current","status_note":"Strategic investment agreed February 2026 alongside existing investor Linden Capital Partners","asset_class":"Private equity","value_creation_plan":"Cinven and Linden will partner with Regenity's management to build on its record of developing and commercialising innovative products, with Cinven drawing on its pan-European presence to support growth in the region; the investment is expected to help scale product development and delivery as the company expands its manufacturing footprint.","value_creation_source_url":"https://www.cinven.com/news-insights/regenity-biosciences-announcement/","notes":"Announced 2026-02-12; financial terms not disclosed; subject to customary regulatory approvals at announcement. Cinven lists Regenity in its portfolio. Stake size not stated, so deal type left blank. Cinven lead: Julia Kahr, Partner and Head of the North America Regional team."}},{"name":"El Jannah","website":"https://eljannah.com.au/","description":"El Jannah is an Australian charcoal chicken restaurant brand, founded in Granville, Western Sydney in 1998, serving charcoal-grilled chicken with its signature toum (garlic sauce) across around 50 restaurants.","sector":"Consumer","subsector":"Quick-service restaurants (charcoal chicken)","country":"Australia","founded_year":1998,"business_model":"B2C restaurants (company-run and franchise)","email":"enquiries@eljannah.com.au","email_type":"generic","leaders":[{"role":"ceo","name":"Brett Houldin","title":"CEO","source_url":"https://eljannah.com.au/whats-on/offers/el-jannah-confirms-national-growth-plans-and-strategic-investment-partnership/","source_kind":"company","evidence":"El Jannah CEO Brett Houldin will continue to lead the business, supported by the Estephan family and General Atlantic."}],"notes":"Founded by Andre and Carole Estephan; first restaurant in Granville, Western Sydney (1998). Grew from five restaurants in 2020 to 50 at the November 2025 announcement, with 160,000 transactions a week across Sydney, Melbourne, Canberra, Wollongong and the Southern Highlands. General Atlantic's site files it under Southeast Asia region, but the business is Australian. No employee count, revenue or EBITDA disclosed by the company or GA.","sources":{"description":{"url":"https://eljannah.com.au/whats-on/offers/el-jannah-confirms-national-growth-plans-and-strategic-investment-partnership/","name":"El Jannah","kind":"company","as_of":"2025-11-28","evidence":"From a humble charcoal chicken shop opened by Lebanese migrant couple Andre and Carole Estephan in Western Sydney in 1998, El Jannah has quickly developed into an Australian cultural institution."},"founded_year":{"url":"https://eljannah.com.au/about-us/","name":"El Jannah","kind":"company","as_of":null,"evidence":"The first El Jannah opened in Granville, Western Sydney, in 1998"},"country":{"url":"https://eljannah.com.au/whats-on/offers/el-jannah-confirms-national-growth-plans-and-strategic-investment-partnership/","name":"El Jannah","kind":"company","as_of":"2025-11-28","evidence":"El Jannah has grown its number of restaurants from five to 50, with 160,000 transactions occur every week across Sydney, Melbourne, Canberra, Wollongong and the Southern Highlands."},"business_model":{"url":"https://eljannah.com.au/","name":"El Jannah","kind":"company","as_of":null,"evidence":"with new El Jannah restaurants opening their doors Australia-wide. Learn more about our franchise opportunities and careers."},"email":{"url":"https://eljannah.com.au/contact/","name":"El Jannah","kind":"company","as_of":null,"evidence":"you can contact our experienced Customer Service Team at enquiries@eljannah.com.au"}},"holding":{"sponsor":"General Atlantic","status":"current","status_note":"Significant investment announced November 2025; listed as a current GA investment (2026)","asset_class":"Growth equity","value_creation_plan":"General Atlantic's investment backs a national expansion to quadruple El Jannah from 50 to almost 200 restaurants (more than 25 openings in NSW, Victoria and the ACT in the next 12 months), deeper digital and guest-experience capability, and selective international expansion, including the Middle East.","value_creation_source_url":"https://eljannah.com.au/whats-on/offers/el-jannah-confirms-national-growth-plans-and-strategic-investment-partnership/","notes":"Announced by El Jannah on 2025-11-28; GA's site lists the investment year as 2026, sector Consumer. CEO Brett Houldin continues with the Estephan family. Stake size and price not stated by the company or GA (press reports of a ~A$1bn majority deal not used), so deal type left blank. GA lead: Neal Kok, Managing Director and Head of Southeast Asia & Australia."}},{"name":"Cloudsmith","website":"https://cloudsmith.com/","description":"Cloudsmith is a fully-managed, cloud-native platform for controlling, securing and distributing software artifacts, giving engineering teams the infrastructure to manage, secure and govern every package across every format and environment.","sector":"Software","subsector":"DevOps / artifact management and software supply chain security","country":"United Kingdom","founded_year":2016,"business_model":"B2B SaaS","email":"contact@cloudsmith.com","email_type":"generic","employees":130,"employees_text":"The company currently has 130 staff, mainly based in Belfast.","employees_as_of":"2026-04-23","leaders":[{"role":"ceo","name":"Glenn Weinstein","title":"CEO","source_url":"https://cloudsmith.com/company/about","source_kind":"company","evidence":"Meet our leadership team | Glenn Weinstein | CEO"},{"role":"cfo","name":"Mark O’Connor","title":"Chief Financial Officer","source_url":"https://cloudsmith.com/company/about","source_kind":"company","evidence":"Mark O’Connor | Chief Financial Officer"},{"role":"other","name":"Alan Carson","title":"CSO and Co-Founder","source_url":"https://cloudsmith.com/company/about","source_kind":"company","evidence":"Alan Carson | CSO and Co-Founder"},{"role":"other","name":"Lee Skillen","title":"CTO and Co-Founder","source_url":"https://cloudsmith.com/company/about","source_kind":"company","e